		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=2441#p2441"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Non, ça ne marche pas : voici le contenu de pg_hba.conf <br />local&#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;postgres&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ident sameuser<br /># TYPE&#160; DATABASE&#160; &#160; USER&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; CIDR-ADDRESS&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; METHOD<br /># &quot;local&quot; is for Unix domain socket connections only<br />local&#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ident sameuser<br /># IPv4 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ident sameuser<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;0.0.0.0/0&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;md5</p>]]></content>
